# PostPylot — Architecture & Stack

## Monorepo Layout

```text
postpylot/
  apps/web/src/          # Next.js App Router PWA
  apps/worker/src/       # Background jobs, rendering, publishing
  packages/db/           # Prisma schema
  packages/ai/           # Gemini, OpenAI, prompts, safety
  packages/platforms/    # youtube, tiktok, linkedin, facebook
  packages/shared/       # types, constants, utils
```

**Hybrid monorepo** — packages by concern (above) plus domain folders inside the web app
(e.g. `lib/brands` + `components/brands`). Do NOT rewrite the web app into `src/features/*`.
Cross-cutting logic that both web and worker need lives in a package; web-only logic lives
in the app's domain folders. See [ADR 004](../../docs/adr/004-architecture-hybrid-monorepo.md).

Today only `apps/web` and `packages/db` exist. Create the other packages/worker as their
phases arrive; evolve into this structure incrementally.

## Stack

| Layer | Choice |
|-------|--------|
| Framework | Next.js 16 (App Router), React 19, TypeScript. Do NOT downgrade to 15 |
| Package manager | npm workspaces (not pnpm — [ADR 003](../../docs/adr/003-package-manager-npm.md)) |
| Frontend | Tailwind, shadcn/ui, Lucide |
| Animation (landing) | Motion (Framer Motion), GSAP, Lenis, typewriter-effect, react-countup |
| Animation (dashboard) | Subtle Motion only |
| Deferred UI | Lottie (empty states), Rive (onboarding), Konva (thumbnail editor), command palette — phase-gated |
| Backend | Route Handlers (OAuth, webhooks, jobs) + Server Actions (UI mutations); Supabase, Prisma, PostgreSQL |
| Jobs | pg-boss on the existing Postgres; separate worker process. No cron in the app runtime — pg-boss owns schedules; GitHub Actions only as an early external trigger if ever needed ([ADR 001](../../docs/adr/001-jobs-pg-boss.md)) |
| AI | `@google/genai` primary, `openai` fallback (Anthropic later) |
| Images | Satori, @resvg/resvg-js, Sharp (template-based; no paid image APIs in MVP) |
| Video | Remotion, FFmpeg (worker only) |
| Voice / Captions | Piper → Kokoro (self-host), ElevenLabs opt-in premium; local Whisper for captions ([ADR 002](../../docs/adr/002-tts-piper-kokoro.md)) |
| Charts | recharts |

## Worker Responsibilities (never in frontend)

Scheduled jobs, AI batch generation, image/thumbnail render, voice-over, video render, platform publish, analytics collection, retry logic.

## AI Agents (structured functions in MVP)

Nine focused agents: Research, Topic, Writer, Image, Voice, Video, Publishing, Analytics,
Quality Control. Fold short-form/YouTube-script generation into Writer, and thumbnails into
Image, to avoid agent sprawl. See the agent table in
[`docs/CONSTITUTION.md`](../../docs/CONSTITUTION.md).

Return **structured JSON** when the app needs fields — not unstructured prose.

## Platform Services

Each file in `packages/platforms/` exposes:

`connectAccount()`, `refreshToken()`, `publishPost()`, `publishVideo()`, `getAnalytics()`, `disconnectAccount()`

Return typed unsupported responses instead of random throws.

## Environment Variables

Maintain `.env.example` with: `DATABASE_URL`, `DIRECT_URL`, Supabase keys, `GEMINI_API_KEY`, `OPENAI_API_KEY`, `TOKEN_ENCRYPTION_SECRET`, OAuth creds per platform, `WEB_PUSH_*`, `APP_URL`, `NODE_ENV`. Validate on startup with `@t3-oss/env-nextjs`. Never commit `.env`.

## Development Behavior

- Work incrementally; small complete changes; match existing conventions.
- Server components by default; client components only for interactivity.
- Business logic in `lib/`, `packages/`, or services — not UI components.
- Validate API inputs with Zod; log errors without leaking secrets.
